# Remote computer-vision analysis provider (optional) — vendor TBD; no CV vendor is under
# contract today. While unset, the /analysis flow uses the local questionnaire-based model.
# When set, QuestionsScreen and AccountScans POST the uploaded photos + questionnaire to this
# endpoint via src/domain/analysis/remoteAnalysisAdapter.ts (confirm that adapter's
# request/response contract against the real vendor's API docs before going live).
# Enabling this sends visitor photos to a third party — marketing.legal.privacy.s2.body and
# s5.body (EN+HE, src/i18n/messages/{en,he}.ts) must be updated to disclose it before this is
# ever set in a deployed environment.
VITE_CV_PROVIDER_API_URL=
VITE_CV_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# HairHealth.ai rescan widget (a Landbot Fullpage embed) — optional.
# Confirmed 2026-09-08 (Pratik, WhatsApp): HairHealth.ai will provide this link once ROOTÉ's
# "patient portal" exists (it does — /account). While unset, the rescan page renders the same
# "not yet connected" placeholder. Results land in ROOTÉ's HubSpot the same one-way way as the
# initial scan — showing any of that data in this app requires a backend this repo doesn't have
# yet (reading HubSpot's API, keyed by the user's email) — that part is NOT built, this env var
# only controls whether the embed itself loads.
VITE_LANDBOT_RESCAN_CONFIG_URL=
